  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A normal is drawn at the point $P$ to the parabola $y^2=8 x$, which is inclined at $60^{\\circ}$ with the straight line $y=8$. Then the point $P$ lies on the straight line",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "dl2mH",
      "text": "\r\n$2 x+y-12-4 \\sqrt{3}=0$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "vrzcE",
      "text": "\r\n$2 x-y-12+4 \\sqrt{3}=0$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xbuOo",
      "text": "\r\n$2 x-y-12-4 \\sqrt{3}=0$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ffl1u",
      "text": "\r\nNone of these",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For the parabola $y^2=4 a x$, the equation of normal at $P\\left(a m^2,-2 a m\\right)$ is $y=m x-2 a m-a m^3$.\r\nHere, $m=\\tan 60^{\\circ}=\\sqrt{3}$\r\n$\\therefore P \\equiv\\left(a(\\sqrt{3})^2,-2 a(\\sqrt{3})\\right) \\equiv(6,-4 \\sqrt{3}) \\quad(\\because a=2)$\r\nThus, $P$ satisfies $2 x-y-12-4 \\sqrt{3}=0$",
    "image": null
  },
